{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "A destructive event that struck Aimia, an island nation of Roshar.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Before the scouring",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "One of the Silver Kingdoms, Aimia had an Oathgate on Akinah island. Fabrials made its islands lush enough to be a paradise.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The other Silver Kingdoms thought Aimia odd, but it stayed close to the Knights Radiant.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The scouring",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "113" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Soon after the Recreance, the other kingdoms turned on Aimia, wanting its fabrials and lanceryn. The invaders wrecked the fabrials that kept the islands alive, and the cold and harsh storms came back.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Having relied on the Radiants to protect them, the Aimians had no real army, and many died. Human survivors fled to lands near Alm, while the Siah Aimians left to wander elsewhere on Roshar.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thinking the lanceryn extinct, most of the Sleepless took on guarding the islands, above all the Dawnshard mural on Akinah, believing its secrets could bring about the end of worlds.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In Mythica, Hessi suggests that Dai-Gonarthis might have caused the scouring.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "113" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Aftermath",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "36" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "6" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The invaders looted what they could and left. Without the fabrials most of Aimia's wildlife died off: the lanceryn were thought extinct and the larkin nearly so, and anything from Aimia, Soulcasters included, became rare.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "36" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Storm-battered and impossible to reach by ship, Aimia was cut off from the rest of Roshar, and the Oathgate on Akinah no longer works.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "36" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Rumours and superstitions about the islands spread across Roshar, kept alive whenever Aimians like Axies the Collector or Arclomedarian are seen. Descendants of Aimia's humans live in Alm and wear their beards like the people of nearby Steen.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "edgedancer", "chapter": "6" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "9" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sailors still try to reach Aimia, drawn by tales of treasure, but the Sleepless warn them off, and a strange storm tends to wreck ships that try.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Sleepless ringed Akinah with forty-foot Soulcast stone spikes and built a decoy city over the buried Oathgate. When a ship got close, they stepped in themselves with sabotage or murder.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They kept the islands' secrets for centuries, until they reached an agreement with Rysn Ftori on the 1174 expedition to Akinah.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-4" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "19" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
